his and so i think one of the  first and most important things is a  lesson right there from harry potter and  the deathly hallows don't try and be  something you're not with the deathly  hallows video game they essentially took  what was an adventure title and made it  into a shooter title instead which i  don't care about the change in setting  you absolutely cannot do that the series  has always been about the adventure the  story the lore and so essentially taking  all of that and turning it into nothing  more than a shooter was definitely a bad  move now the good news here is we  already know that hogwarts legacy is not  doing this now what we don't know though  is what the balance is like we've seen  combat and i know that some people seem  excited about it some people aren't so  excited about it based on what we've  seen so far i personally think it looks  pretty good a lot of people have talked  about how the enemies don't really  appear to attack in more than groups of  just one person at a time but my hope  here is that the demo we saw was  basically on the lowest difficulty set  and we know there's going to be multiple  difficulties of course they could just  be showcasing things for the purposes of  that demo as well we don't know that  that's exactly how it's going to play  and we also frankly don't know how the  combat is going to feel that's really  the main thing right how does it flow as  you're actually playing the game and  interacting with all of these enemies  now on the more positive side some of  the most beloved harry potter games are  the first three so sorcerer's stone  chamber of secrets and prisoner of  azkaban now i've seen people kind of  disagree on whether they prefer the pc  or the console versions but regardless  of which one you like better it was  really that exploration and that sense  of discovery from those games that  people liked so much honestly i would  have enjoyed chamber of secrets on the  gamecube even more if it wasn't for all  the loading screens that interrupt you  almost every time you go into a new room  go to a new area so that's kind of  annoying hopefully we won't have to  worry about a lot of load screens with  hogwarts legacy so i really hope that  hogwarts legacy goes all in on that  sense of exploration now they're saying  the right things in the developer behind  the scenes that aired at the end of the  state of play they absolutely seemed  like they get it and that is one thing  that i really took from that state of  play more than anything else is that i  do feel like the developers and the  people working on this game truly get  what has made for a good harry potter  game in some cases of the previous games  and also what hasn't made for such a  great game they really seem to get that  hogwarts is sort of the central hub for  everything hogwarts they have to nail  that experience for it all to be  worthwhile right so embrace that lore of  hogwarts embrace the secret passages  embrace the four hogwarts common rooms  and the houses which again from what  we've seen so far it totally seems like  they are embracing these things and  specifically when it comes to the lore i  think there's a very interesting balance  here because when i was watching the  movies originally as a kid i was so  disappointed when they made any little  change and over time i started to  understand some of those changes and  still to this day there are some changes  that drive me crazy anytime i see the  movies on tv and this is just going to  always be the case with any sort of  beloved property they have to strike a  very careful balance here of embracing  the lore embracing some things that are  established in canon but also trying to  do some new things and i would never  advocate for completely breaking the  cannon that's just not in me i can't do  it but in some cases i am okay with them  kind of bending the canon just a little  bit if it makes for a better video game  experience and trut